Package: pgphenotype
Title: Phenotypes in Pedigrees on a Rust Core
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ryan", "Waples", email = "ryan.waples@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Authors of the bundled Rust crates", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "see inst/AUTHORS in the source tarball"))
Description: Methods for phenotypes measured on the members of a pedigree,
    computed by the Rust core shared with the 'pg-phenotype' Python package.
    The first method is PA-FGRS family genetic risk scores from one or two
    binary traits.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc (>= 1.85)
Copyright: Ryan Waples for the package; the bundled Rust crates in
    src/rust/vendor.tar.xz are copyright their authors, listed with their
    licenses in inst/AUTHORS.
URL: https://github.com/rwaples/pg-phenotype
BugReports: https://github.com/rwaples/pg-phenotype/issues
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
